1
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:36,320
Makazaki.

2
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:38,280
Here.

3
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:44,360
If I were you, I'd take a seat.

4
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:45,220
Yes, sir.

5
00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:50,380
Sora?

6
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:00,540
It's been a while, Taka.

7
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:07,060
This is the first time we've really seen each other in ten long years.

8
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:12,000
Which included France and the Holy Roman Empire.

9
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:15,640
I remember that day he first transferred here.

10
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:19,040
It was right around our seasonal uniform change.

11
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:24,020
Hello.

12
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:27,500
I'm, uh, the transfer student.

13
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:29,140
Okay, great.

14
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:30,580
My name is Kodaka.

15
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:32,900
Nice to be here.

16
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:37,200
Oh no, Ms. Osada.

17
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:38,220
Did he just attack her?

18
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:38,880
Deliquent much?

19
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:39,420
He's new here.

20
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:40,440
What's up with his hair?

21
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,040
Taka.

22
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:53,180
It's Taka.

23
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,760
I'd recognize that hair and expression anywhere.

24
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:57,500
It's definitely him.

25
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:01,160
He hasn't changed a bit in the last ten years.

26
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,860
He always did suck at smiling.

27
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:08,840
And the harder he tried to be nice and friendly to people, the more it would just backfire on him.

28
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:11,340
I can't believe it.

29
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:15,060
Oh, I forgot my book.

30
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:19,560
Here, take mine.

31
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,120
Oh, thanks.

32
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,780
Yeah, that's him.

33
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:31,280
It's Taka.

34
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:35,960
My one and only friend when I was a kid.

35
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:41,200
He didn't even notice me.

36
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:45,580
Well, tell me what you think, Tomo.

37
00:03:46,980 --> 00:03:47,380
Yeah.

38
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:48,260
Taka.

39
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,540
Or Kodaka Hasegawa.

40
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:54,680
My best friend from back when I was a kid who doesn't even remember who I am now.

41
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:56,160
Isn't that the worst?

42
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,080
Yeah.

43
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:02,940
My best guess is that it's because I used to dress like a boy whenever we hung out together.

44
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:05,100
And yeah, I get that, but still.

45
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:06,560
No way!

46
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:08,860
Why should I have to be the one to talk to him?

47
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,480
I mean, think about it.

48
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:13,140
I have no idea how to start a conversation with somebody.

49
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:16,840
I don't know.

50
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,620
I thought maybe I could get him to talk to me first.

51
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:30,860
When I get to school, when I leave the class after school, when I put things in my locker,

52
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:35,220
or take them back out, I always have to walk by him.

53
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:39,120
But he never says a single word to me.

54
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:42,680
It's not like that at all.

55
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:44,380
What do you mean it's my fault?

56
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:45,520
Right.

57
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:46,180
Yeah.

58
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:47,300
And you know what, Tomo?

59
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:48,780
You make a really good point.

60
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,500
Do you want to go shopping after school?

61
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:52,680
I need some eyeliner.

62
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:53,120
Sure.

63
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:55,400
Let's try that makeup place across from the station.

64
00:04:55,780 --> 00:04:57,360
I think I do remember that.

65
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:04,080
No, I can't believe this!

66
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:05,060
Crap!

67
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:06,600
Kodaka saw me.

68
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:07,940
Could he hear me talking?

69
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:09,480
I'm gonna die.

70
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:12,040
Please don't tell me you heard what I was saying.

71
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:13,140
This is bad.

72
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,320
This is really bad.

73
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,400
What do I do?

74
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,340
What do you want?

75
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:27,400
I was just wondering, do you like to see ghosts and stuff?

76
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:28,200
What?

77
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:30,980
Uh, no, because ghosts don't exist.

78
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:32,920
Well then, who have you been talking to?

79
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:34,280
You were watching me?

80
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:34,300
You were watching me?

81
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:46,140
Look, I was having a conversation with my best friend ever.

82
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:47,720
She's made her air, okay?

83
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:54,660
And that was the first conversation I had had with Taka in ten years.

84
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:56,480
Also, I'm an idiot.

85
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,480
That's perfect.

86
00:05:57,480 --> 00:06:01,500
That's perfect.

87
00:06:01,940 --> 00:06:02,700
A club!

88
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:03,560
Huh?

89
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:10,500
See you later, Kodaka.

90
00:06:13,940 --> 00:06:14,680
That's it.

91
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:15,980
I'll start a club.

92
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:18,900
Here's a new club application for you.

93
00:06:19,460 --> 00:06:20,660
Thank you so much, sir.

94
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:33,260
If I'm not in a club, I can make one.

95
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:37,220
A club just for me and Kodaka.

96
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:48,020
Sometimes I use this chapel when I need a quiet place to read, or when the library's too crowded

97
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:48,680
for me to focus.

98
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,160
It's always really comforting.

99
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:56,160
Sister Maria Takeyama is supposed to be in charge of this room.

100
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:58,620
Apparently, she's still a child.

101
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,760
I guess it's good I don't hate kids.

102
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,440
Excuse me.

103
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:12,860
Hey, you!

104
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:14,660
Why the hell are you in here?

105
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:17,220
This is my holy room for napping, so get out!

106
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:19,760
It's not a place for scummy sinners like you!

107
00:07:19,760 --> 00:07:27,760
Um, hi, my name is Yosara Mikazuki, and I'm from Class 2-5.

108
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:30,160
If you're Sister Maria, I'm supposed to ask you...

109
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:30,720
Forget it!

110
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:32,920
What a little brat!

111
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:37,020
Okay, I think if you just heard me out, you'd say that...

112
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:38,260
I don't listen to poopy heads!

113
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,460
Oh, you're gonna listen.

114
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:45,140
I'm applying to start a new after-school club, and I was hoping I could use this room.

115
00:07:45,140 --> 00:07:45,980
No means no!

116
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:48,040
Now get out of here, you grody plop of poop!

117
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:59,640
It's time.

118
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,320
Kodaka, follow me, please.

119
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:10,100
Holy crap, she talked to him.

120
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,420
To that Hasekawa creep?

121
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,940
Now, let the clubbing begin.

122
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:17,700
Our purpose can be to help us make friends.

123
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:18,960
Perfect.

124
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:20,760
A club for me and Kodaka.

125
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:22,420
Taka and Sora.

126
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:26,900
This way, we'll be able to become friends again like we used to be.

127
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:34,060
Now, let's see.

128
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:46,640
How often should we open your patience?

129
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:48,640
Oh

130
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:18,640
Oh

131
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:51,860
Hey, Asagawa

132
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:55,280
Why is he staring at Yuzuru like that?

133
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,260
They're still standing

134
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:56,900
Hello

135
00:09:56,900 --> 00:10:05,780
All right, moving on with attendance

136
00:10:05,780 --> 00:10:06,700
Miyajimi

137
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:07,100
Here

138
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,000
Butto

139
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:08,580
Here

140
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:09,400
Yagashi

141
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,260
Yagashi

142
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:13,080
Sorry, yeah, I'm here

143
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:13,420
Good

144
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:14,660
Yamazaki

145
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:15,160
Here

146
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:27,080
That's when I said

147
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:31,820
So, um, hey

148
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:33,320
Hey, what?

149
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,940
I was just, what happened to your hair?

150
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:36,920
Got it cut?

151
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:39,040
Yeah, well, I can kind of see that

152
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:41,360
But, like, why did you cut it?

153
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:43,460
Blame that summer festival night

154
00:10:43,460 --> 00:10:46,480
But that was just the tip, right?

155
00:10:46,840 --> 00:10:48,660
It's not like the whole thing got destroyed

156
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:50,340
You didn't have to cut off so much

157
00:10:50,340 --> 00:10:51,840
I did have to cut this mud off

158
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,340
Because you totally soaked my head

159
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:55,520
No matter how many times I washed my hair

160
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:57,620
That freaking stench would not come out

161
00:10:57,620 --> 00:10:59,540
Oh, I'm really sorry

162
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:00,680
Please, I, uh

163
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:01,540
Soaked her head?

164
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:04,300
He said just the tip, but did he force her?

165
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:06,060
Yeah, that is not cool

166
00:11:06,060 --> 00:11:07,020
She washed and washed

167
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:09,360
But couldn't get the gross stink of his stuff out of her hair

168
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:10,900
You're wrong

169
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:12,940
I was only doing what had to be done

170
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:14,920
Shut up and come on

171
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:16,220
Wait, what?

172
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:16,940
Yozora

173
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:24,380
Okay

174
00:11:24,380 --> 00:11:27,320
I, uh

175
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:29,460
What I'm trying to say is

176
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:31,320
You're right, okay?

177
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:32,080
I was Sora

178
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,840
So what are you thinking?

179
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,260
I'm, uh

180
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:37,480
Pretty surprised

181
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:38,760
And anything else?

182
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:39,740
Like what?

183
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,380
You know, like else

184
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:43,240
Like, are you happy?

185
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:44,480
Maybe honored?

186
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:46,040
Or are you moved at all?

187
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,800
Hmm, how do I put it?

188
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,520
I'm bewildered by the whole thing

189
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:50,700
Surprised

190
00:11:50,700 --> 00:11:53,300
Yeah, that's definitely the strongest feeling right now

191
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,300
Oh

192
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:57,260
That haircut does look really good on you

193
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:59,660
Uh, uh, um

194
00:11:59,660 --> 00:12:00,820
Thanks

195
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:02,120
You don't think it's weird?

196
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:03,580
No

197
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:05,240
It's nice

198
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:05,620
Oh

199
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:07,140
Thank you

200
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:10,480
I actually went to a hair salon

201
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:11,660
Wow

202
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:13,180
That must have been fun

203
00:12:13,180 --> 00:12:14,700
Was it what you expected?

204
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:16,020
I was nervous

205
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:17,940
Yeah, I can imagine that you were

206
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:20,200
Hold on a sec

207
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:22,620
You knew who I was the day I transferred here?

208
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:23,180
Yep

209
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:24,640
I knew from the very beginning

210
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:26,680
And I'm surprised yet again

211
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:27,960
Don't be

212
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:30,020
I'd recognize your pudding head anywhere

213
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:31,260
Thank you

214
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:33,200
Well, you certainly could have fooled me

215
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:34,020
Wait

216
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:36,980
But don't you remember that day when we met in the classroom?

217
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:40,160
I swear you said something about not remembering what my name was

218
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:40,900
Hmm

219
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:44,040
I was pretty irritated that I recognized who you were

220
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:45,960
Even though you didn't have a clue about me

221
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:48,180
So you pretended you didn't know me instead?

222
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:48,980
That's right

223
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:51,280
Crap, we're at a dead end

224
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:54,200
I'm sorry if I seemed rude

225
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:57,340
But, I mean, how can you blame me for that?

226
00:12:57,340 --> 00:13:00,560
It's not like I'd ever seen you wearing a skirt, right?

227
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,840
You were only ever dressed like a boy

228
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,500
Who cares what I wore?

229
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:07,120
I never once told you I was a boy when we were kids

230
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:11,000
Sorry, it's just you don't normally see girls wearing boys' clothes

231
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,400
And picking fights with other boys whenever they could

232
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:17,200
I was going to tell you I was a girl

233
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,600
But you up and disappeared before I got the chance to

234
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:22,520
Are you serious?

235
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:25,080
That was the important thing you said you were going to tell me?

236
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:28,420
But you never showed up that day

237
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:29,240
And I waited

238
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,240
A long time

239
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:30,880
You're wrong

240
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:32,820
Because I did show up then

241
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:35,260
But I got too embarrassed

242
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:36,660
I was in a skirt

243
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:37,740
And

244
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:40,080
And I was afraid you would laugh at me

245
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:40,740
You what?

246
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:45,740
I wore a skirt because I wanted to confess to you I was a girl

247
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:48,300
I figured that was the best way to let you know

248
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:50,960
But I'd never worn a skirt before

249
00:13:50,960 --> 00:13:53,700
So I didn't know if it looked good on me or not

250
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:56,100
I thought maybe you would laugh at me

251
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,980
I just

252
00:13:57,980 --> 00:14:01,180
I couldn't make myself do it

253
00:14:01,180 --> 00:14:02,600
It was way too embarrassing

254
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:05,180
But if I'd known you were moving

255
00:14:05,180 --> 00:14:08,200
I might have gotten up the courage to actually go for it

256
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:10,220
You see?

257
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:11,760
This whole thing is all your fault

258
00:14:11,760 --> 00:14:12,580
There's no way

259
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:14,960
Because first of all, weirdo

260
00:14:14,960 --> 00:14:17,260
You didn't have to wear a skirt to tell me

261
00:14:17,260 --> 00:14:18,660
Whatever

262
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:20,020
You know for a fact

263
00:14:20,020 --> 00:14:21,060
If I had just told you

264
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:22,360
You never would have believed me

265
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:23,140
Yeah

266
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:24,400
You're probably right

267
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,420
I think

268
00:14:25,420 --> 00:14:26,120
Well

269
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,480
The fact we were friends

270
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:29,200
I mean

271
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:30,740
I think the fact we were acquaintances

272
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:32,600
Should remain a secret from the rest of the club

273
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,360
How come?

274
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:35,140
There's no reason for them to know

275
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:36,140
Uh

276
00:14:36,140 --> 00:14:37,020
Sure

277
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:37,820
That's fine

278
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:38,140
Good

279
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:39,060
Then that's that

280
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:40,360
Okay, let's go

281
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:41,740
One sec

282
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:42,320
Hmm?

283
00:14:42,720 --> 00:14:44,180
I don't know what to call you now

